  - Model Context Protocol
abstract: >-
  After the Agent is an experimental browser instrument for repairing inherited
  configuration and queued work in a simulated light installation. A deterministic
  engine supports browser interaction, a local Model Context Protocol server and
  a headless runner. An independent Python oracle checks repairs against twelve
  fixed future scenarios. The source includes a retained model setup demonstration,
  separately labelled authored fixtures and reproducible software checks. Human
  usability, recovery benefit, learning effects and transfer to production systems
  have not been established. Research collection is disabled.
